# Trivy allowlist — justified exceptions, reviewed 2026-08-05.
#
# Rule: every image in the compose files is pinned at the LATEST release its
# upstream publishes. The findings below have fixed versions upstream, but no
# patched image exists to pin. Ignoring them is the honest alternative to
# inventing a fix that does not exist; it is not permission to relax.
#
# Exposure context: every service binds loopback only, runs with
# no-new-privileges (cap_drop where the service allows it), and telemetry off.
#
# This file must shrink, never grow:
# - security.yml re-scans the same digests weekly, so a CVE fixed in a new
#   release is caught even between PRs;
# - Dependabot (docker-compose ecosystem) proposes the bumps that let entries
#   be deleted here;
# - any new finding fails CI until it is either fixed by a bump or justified
#   in this file with the same rigor.

# --- ollama/ollama:0.33.0 (latest release) ----------------------------------
# Go standard library and golang.org/x/* findings: 38 of them, every one
# with a fixed toolchain or module upstream and none of them carried by a
# rebuilt Ollama image. The 0.33.0 bump (2026-08-21) reports exactly the same
# set 0.32.5 did, scanned side by side — it fixes nothing here and is taken
# because the pinning policy asks for the latest release, not because it
# moves this list. Ollama publishes no host port; its only clients are Reed
# and Open WebUI on the stack's own network. Reviewed 2026-08-26.
