# --- qdrant/qdrant:v1.19.0 (latest release) ---------------------------------
# v1.19.0 (2026-08-05) is still the latest release, so none of these have an
# image to be pinned at. Qdrant publishes no host port; access goes through
# Reed's API or `docker compose exec`. This is the reviewed rescan the
# previous note promised: five entries the v1.18.3 era left behind are gone
# because the images no longer report them, and the Debian base findings that
# appeared since are named below.
#
# - util-linux (CVE-2026-53612 through -53615): a TOCTOU in `mount` and three
#   siblings across the same source package. The container mounts nothing at
#   runtime and runs unprivileged with no-new-privileges.
# - OpenSSL (CVE-2026-14456): unbounded memory growth in the QUIC *server*.
#   Qdrant serves HTTP and gRPC; it never speaks QUIC.
# - js-yaml (GHSA-5p4m-2wfm-xmqj) and nanoid (CVE-2026-67213, -67214) in the
#   dashboard's npm tree: quadratic CPU on crafted YAML, and loops on sizes
#   the dashboard never takes from input. The dashboard has no published port.
#
# Reviewed 2026-08-26.
CVE-2026-14456
CVE-2026-53612
CVE-2026-53613
CVE-2026-53614
CVE-2026-53615
CVE-2026-67213
CVE-2026-67214
GHSA-5p4m-2wfm-xmqj

